<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Where (200)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>where
where &lt;name&gt;
</pre>
<p><b>where</b> alone lists the players in the game: each one's name, the 
title of the room they are in, and in brackets where that is (the room's 
symbolic name, and what they are inside, such as a ship). A god switched 
into a monster is shown "In body of" that monster. You don't see those who 
are invisible to a higher level than yours.
</p><p><b>where &lt;name&gt;</b> finds everything in the world by that name: players, 
monsters and things, each with its room and where it is. Up to 100 are 
listed, and a count follows. Players who are not yet playing show as 
MENU.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Goto</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wpath</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Users</a>
</pre>




</div>